---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import OpenPrinterStatus from '../../components/OpenPrinterStatus.astro';
import openprinter from '../../data/openprinter.json';
---

<SiteLayout
  title="OpenPrinter Status Tracker"
  description="Can you buy OpenPrinter yet? Track the planned autumn 2026 crowdfunding launch, pending price and shipping details, and practical alternatives."
>
  <div class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">OpenPrinter tracker</p>
    <h1>OpenPrinter is interesting. It is not a finished buying option yet.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      The team plans an autumn 2026 crowdfunding launch. Here is what you can buy now, what is still a plan, and which details have not been announced.
    </p>
  </div>

  <article class="article">
    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>Can I buy OpenPrinter now?</h2>
      <p>As checked on September 18, 2026, Crowd Supply still lists the project as “Coming Soon” with an update signup. It does not yet offer a live campaign purchase on that page.</p>
      <h2>When will OpenPrinter launch?</h2>
      <p>The <a href="https://www.crowdsupply.com/open-tools/openprinter/updates/on-the-road-to-launch">September 17 team update</a> targets a crowdfunding launch in autumn 2026. An exact launch date and shipping date have not been announced in the reviewed sources. Crowdfunding launch and delivery are separate milestones.</p>
      <h2>How much will it cost?</h2>
      <p>Final pricing is still pending. The team says it will share pricing, the roadmap, complete specifications, and the official launch date in a future update. We have no verified retail price or delivery estimate to compare with printers available today.</p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section alt">
    <div class="container split">
      <OpenPrinterStatus />
      <div class="panel">
        <div class="panel-inner">
          <p class="eyebrow" style="color: var(--amber);">What to watch</p>
          <h2>Before anyone calls it a replacement</h2>
          <ul class="status-list">
            {openprinter.watchItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="article">
    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>Why the licensing detail matters</h2>
      <p>
        OpenPrinter is often described as open source or open hardware, but the practical buyer question is narrower:
        can normal users repair, modify, and maintain it without being locked into a vendor-controlled supply chain?
        The CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 detail is important because non-commercial terms can limit independent manufacturing and resale.
      </p>
      <div class="callout">
        We treat OpenPrinter as an open-hardware-inspired project under observation, not as a confirmed commercial printer recommendation.
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="article-section">
      <h2>What to buy while waiting</h2>
      <p>
        If you need a printer now, the safer path is to choose a mature no-subscription or refillable model and keep OpenPrinter on a watchlist.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="callout">
        Need a printer now? Read the <a href="/openprinter/alternatives/">OpenPrinter alternatives decision guide</a> or the <a href="/guides/no-subscription-printers/">field-sourced model reviews</a>.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
